 scale="3" id="f-917">28,895</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:0 1pt"/><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-55" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:StandardProductWarrantyAccrualNoncurrent" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="3" id="f-918">30,428</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/></tr></table></div></ix:nonNumeric><div style="margin-top:9pt;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The most significant component of our warranty liability was in the North America segment. As of December 31, 2025, the warranty liability in the North America segment totaled $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-169" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:StandardProductWarrantyAccrual" scale="6" id="f-919">36.4</ix:nonFraction> million, after discounting future estimated cash flows at rates between <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="c-80" decimals="4" name="us-gaap:ProductLiabilityContingencyAccrualDiscountRate" scale="-2" id="f-920">3.55</ix:nonFraction>% and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="c-81" decimals="4" name="us-gaap:ProductLiabilityContingencyAccrualDiscountRate" scale="-2" id="f-921">4.09</ix:nonFraction>%. Without discounting, the liability would have increased by approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-7" decimals="-5" name="jeld:StandardProductWarrantyAccrualDiscountAdjustment" scale="6" id="f-922">2.8</ix:nonFraction> million.</span></div></ix:continuation><div id="if5186a3dc11d4fd3bff2957bff6646b9_124"></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 12. <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:DebtDisclosureTextBlock" id="f-923" continuedAt="f-923-1" escape="true">Long-Term Debt</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="f-923-1" continuedAt="f-923-2"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c-1" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfDebtInstrumentsTextBlock" id="f-924" continuedAt="f-924-1" escape="true"><div style="margin-top:9pt;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Our long-term debt, net of original issue discounts and unamortized debt issuance costs, consisted of the following:</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt;text-align:center"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:99.861%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:48.135%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:15.728%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.495%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:15.450%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.495%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:14.897%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding: